<title>UK: ATHLETICS-MEN'S 3,000 METRES EVOLUTION.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-MEN'S 3,000 METRES EVOLUTION.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Evolution of the men's 3,000</p>
<p>metres world record since 1956 (tabulate under - time, name,</p>
<p>nationality, date):</p>
<p> 7:55.6   Gordon Pirie (Britain)		  1956</p>
<p> 7:52.8   Pirie					 1956</p>
<p> 7:49.2   Michel Jazy (France)		    1962</p>
<p> 7:49.0   Jazy					  1965</p>
<p> 7:46.0   Siegfried Herrmann (West Germany)   1965</p>
<p> 7:39.6   Kip Keino (Kenya)			 1965</p>
<p> 7:37.6   Emiel Puttemans (Belgium)	     1972</p>
<p> 7:35.2   Brendan Foster (Britain)		1974</p>
<p> 7:32.1   Henry Rono (Kenya)			1978</p>
<p> 7:29.45  Said Aouita (Morocco)		   1989</p>
<p> 7:28.96  Moses Kiptanui (Kenya)		  16.8.92</p>
<p> 7:25.11  Noureddine Morceli (Algeria)	  2.8.94</p>
<p> 7:20.67  Daniel Komen (Kenya)		    1.9.96</p>
